{
  "info": {
    "name": "Events Service API",
    "description": "Complete API collection for Events Service (events, sessions, courses, registrations, certificates, filter templates). All routes under /api require authentication (either a gateway-forwarded JWT, or a direct Bearer token if AUTH_BYPASS is not enabled). GET /health and GET /api are unauthenticated.\n\nRegistration/approval workflow (see Registrations folder): creating a registration never creates or links a Profile and never captures/posts payment - it only records a duplicate-detection verdict (duplicateReview.status: EXACT_MATCH | CONFIRMED_LINK | POTENTIAL_MATCH | NO_MATCH) and leaves the registration at approvalStatus 'pending_review'. A Profile is only created/linked, and payment only captured (Stripe) or posted to the GL (manual/comp/invoice), when a CRM user explicitly calls PUT /registrations/:id/approve - for a POTENTIAL_MATCH verdict this call must include a decision ('LINK' with candidateProfileId, or 'CREATE_NEW'). PUT /registrations/:id/reject releases the Stripe authorization (or voids the recorded-but-unposted manual/comp/invoice payment) and cancels the registration instead - no case auto-approves.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4011",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "authToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "eventId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "courseId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "registrationId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "profileId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "templateId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
